{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show a clear uptrend, add an upward bias that grows with horizon (small at 1–3d, large by 10–30d).",
    "Horizon-dependent drift error: the model’s forecast path is too flat/mean-reverting; apply a positive slope correction proportional to recent trend (e.g., extrapolate part of the last 10–15d momentum).",
    "Lag after regime shift: following a breakout to new highs, the model adjusts too slowly; override with faster catch-up (raise the next ~7–14 days toward the new level).",
    "Systematic underestimation of volatility/upside tails: peaks are capped ~5–15 EUR below realized levels; widen the upper range by lifting forecasts more on high-momentum days.",
    "Late-horizon anchoring: beyond ~15–20 days, forecasts revert toward ~69–72 despite outcomes staying >78–84; reduce mean-reversion strength when trend strength/level shift is detected.",
    "Asymmetry: errors are predominantly negative (forecast < outcome) across most horizons; apply a baseline positive bias even without strong trend, then scale it up with trend/acceleration."
  ]
}
